2026-11-15: `src/kernels/nav/mls_core` provides the dependency-free Rust surface
and graph core with a C ABI bridge. On the fixed arrival-box map, after matching
DimOS floor step conversion, the native Rust graph reports 29 nodes, 45 edges,
and 2 components. Its filtered corridors pass the C++ body, support, step,
slope, and continuous sweep checks. The Rust artifact is still an A/B boundary
because endpoint query, stable CellId, regional update, cache restore, and the
prepared artifact contract have not moved into Rust. The migration order is
documented in docs/design/mls-rust-migration-20261115.md.

The first owning `PreparedArtifactHandle` adapter now covers artifact creation,
surface/graph export, graph-only query, region update and revision ownership.
This is a migration seam, not a production backend switch.
